cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis, data, tables or figures, cite this release and credit Bodytype.org with a link to https://bodytype.org."
title: "When a centimeter changes the label: boundary sensitivity in a body type calculator"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic sensitivity analysis of Bodytype's v2 four-girth body type
  classification rules on a synthetic rule-space grid of 669,858 tested
  points. The release reports how often single-field shifts of ±0.5 cm, ±1 cm
  and ±2 cm change the label, how close tested points sit to a rule boundary,
  which thresholds are crossed, and how rounding affects labels. It is not a
  population sample, an accuracy study, a measurement-error model or medical
  data. The analysis code is released under the MIT License; synthetic data,
  tables and figures are released under CC BY 4.0. Any use must credit
  Bodytype.org and link to https://bodytype.org.
